# Journey has no command line: the whole interface is read_char
# (§15), driven from ZIL's PARTY-INPUT loop. The vocabulary below:
# a letter presses the first letter of a visible command (that is
# the COMMAND-CHR every command carries), a bare > presses return
# to activate the bolded default, <space> cycles the highlight
# between the party column and the character grid -- the gateway
# key, since letters only reach the commands of the mode the
# highlight is in -- and the arrows walk the grid when two
# characters offer the same first letter. Recorded through the
# opening chapter: Lavos, Garlimon's hut, the flash flood, and
# into the cave under Sunrise Mountain -- the release-gate slice;
# the deep game is post-1.0 expedition country.

# The boot questions: no saved game, two title pages.
